{
  "name": "Annual start-of-year SPX implied volatility proxy from Cboe VIX",
  "description": "First available Cboe VIX closing level of each calendar year, converted from percentage points to decimal annualized volatility. Used as an at-the-money volatility proxy for one-year European put pricing. Years before 1990 use the median of these observations as an explicit fallback.",
  "source": "https://cdn.cboe.com/api/global/us_indices/daily_prices/VIX_History.csv",
  "sourceName": "Cboe Volatility Index (VIX) historical daily closes",
  "methodologyNotes": [
    "VIX measures approximately 30-day expected SPX volatility, not one-year put implied volatility.",
    "Each annual observation uses the first trading-day VIX close of that calendar year.",
    "Values are stored as decimals (for example 0.1724 for a VIX close of 17.24).",
    "Pre-1990 historical return years use fallbackImpliedVol because no official VIX history exists before 1990."
  ],
